<title>USA: Inland backs Q2 EPS estimate of $0.63.</title>
<headline>Inland backs Q2 EPS estimate of $0.63.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Inland Steel Industries Inc chief executive Robert Darnall said the company is comforable with the First Call 1997 second quarter consensus earnings estimate of about $0.63 a share.</p>
<p>&quot;I'm comfortable with that. It's in the right range,&quot; Darnall told Reuters after the steelmaker's annual meeting here on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The company earned $0.35 a share in the 1996 second quarter.  </p>
<p>That year-ago figure included two non-recurring items. Excluding those items, the steelmaker earned $0.25 per share.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
